<!-- 3. CHALLENGE -->
<section class="slide-page" id="challenge">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 · Context</span>
      <h2>The problem was bigger than building 12 applications</h2>
      <p>Banks operate in complex environments. The suite required deep domain capabilities while remaining configurable and integration-ready.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="story">
        <span class="eyebrow">The challenge</span>
        <h3>One platform had to serve very different banking jobs.</h3>
        <p>Lending, AML, cards, reconciliation, treasury and audit do not share workflows. The challenge was finding reusable patterns without flattening domain complexity.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Coexistence with existing bank systems mattered from day one.</li>
          <li>Institution-specific workflows required configuration over hardcoding.</li>
          <li>Regulated processes required strict roles, maker-checker, and audits.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="story">
        <span class="eyebrow">Product thesis</span>
        <h3>Standardise the platform. Configure the institution. Integrate ecosystems.</h3>
        <p>Approached as a common product foundation with modular domain applications rather than 12 disconnected projects.</p>
        <div class="story-flow">
          <div class="story-step"><b>Standardise</b><span>Roles &amp; controls</span></div>
          <div class="story-step"><b>Configure</b><span>Business rules</span></div>
          <div class="story-step"><b>Integrate</b><span>Bank systems</span></div>
          <div class="story-step"><b>Adopt</b><span>Migration &amp; support</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="challenge-response">
        <div><b>Configure</b><span>Institution journeys without rebuilding code.</span></div>
        <div><b>Integrate</b><span>Bank systems and payment rails seamlessly.</span></div>
        <div><b>Control</b><span>Roles, validations, approvals, traceability.</span></div>
        <div><b>Implement</b><span>Migration, deployment, training readiness.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4. STRATEGY -->
<section class="slide-page alt" id="strategy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · Strategy</span>
      <h2>From application list to a reusable banking ecosystem</h2>
      <p>Connecting platform architecture, domain design, and client adoption to reduce repeated effort while preserving flexibility.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="strategy">
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#9b8cf5"><div class="num">01</div><h3>Platform foundation</h3><p>Reusable roles, permissions, workflow states, and validations before multiplying complexity.</p></div>
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#73cbb4"><div class="num">02</div><h3>Configurable model</h3><p>Separate reusable product behaviour from bank-specific rules for smooth implementation.</p></div>
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#7eb5ed"><div class="num">03</div><h3>Integration-first design</h3><p>Map API contracts, authentications, failures, and reconciliation during early journey design.</p></div>
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#efb785"><div class="num">04</div><h3>Controls by design</h3><p>Translate regulatory constraints into roles, maker-checker states, evidence, and audit trails.</p></div>
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#f49dbd"><div class="num">05</div><h3>Migration awareness</h3><p>Treat legacy data as part of product work: map, transform, validate, and verify post-migration.</p></div>
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#9dcbed"><div class="num">06</div><h3>Two-phase roadmap</h3><p>Build the first six applications in months 0–6, then scale remaining six using foundational lessons.</p></div>
      <div class="strategy-card" style="--tone:#a8d7a8"><div class="num">07</div><h3>Feedback-led build</h3><p>Use progressive product demos and bank feedback to refine workflows and exception handling.</p></div>
